Method add(int index, Role role). It inserts role at index, shifting elements with index >= current position up. The comment:

"@@@ If the index is between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive, and the role is not null, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element was null or equals the old element at that position."

Interpretation: Preconditions: index >=0 && index <= old size (inclusive). role != null.

Postcondition: For every i such that i >= index && i < old size (i from insertion point to old size -1?), the element at position i+1 after insertion (i.e., this.get(i+1)) is either null if old element at i was null, else equals old element at i.

We need to refer to old values using \old. Also need to use this.get(i) etc. The list contains Role objects, but underlying arraylist of Object. Use get method returning Role. Use .equals for non-null? The comment says "equals the old element at that position". So we can assert:

(index >=0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null) => \forall int i; i >= index && i < \old(this.size()); ( (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i+1) == null) || (\old(this.get(i)) != null && this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) ) );

Need to ensure we access old size: \old(this.size()).

Also need to ensure that after insertion, size = old size +1, but not required by comment.

Thus final assert.

